Output shell completions

Writes a completion script for SHELL to stdout.

Have your shell run this command at startup rather than saving its output to a
file. A saved script describes the snouty that wrote it, and goes stale when
`snouty update` installs a new version. If your shell already initializes
completion, add only the snouty line after that initialization. Open a new shell
to load the setup, and again after each update.

For zsh, add this to ~/.zshrc:
  autoload -Uz compinit
  compinit
  source <(snouty completions zsh)

For bash, add this to ~/.bashrc:
  eval "$(snouty completions bash)"

For fish, put this line in ~/.config/fish/completions/snouty.fish:
  snouty completions fish | source

For elvish, add this to ~/.config/elvish/rc.elv:
  if (has-external snouty) { eval (snouty completions elvish | slurp) }

For PowerShell, add this to $PROFILE:
  snouty completions powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression

Usage: snouty completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          Shell to generate completions for
          
          [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --utc
          Show times in UTC instead of the local timezone

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
